# **A measurement input is not code we maintain.** `benchmarks/retrieval-corpus/` is a snapshot of a directory the
# retrieval measurement runs on, and a formatter that reformatted it would change the corpus a recorded figure was
# measured against - the same reason the questions beside it are frozen. It passes `--check` today; the entry is here so
# that a future change to the formatter's opinion cannot silently rewrite the input.
benchmarks/retrieval-corpus/

# **A Java program is not a TypeScript file, and Prettier has no parser for one.** The oracle is formatted by the
# conventions of the language it is written in - which is the point of it being written in that language - so it is
# excluded here rather than reformatted into something neither formatter is right about.
scripts/callgraph-oracle-java/

# **A generated artifact is not formatted by hand, and this one cannot be.** `benchmarks/lca-bug-localization.json` is
# 2.3 MB of per-instance rows written by `scripts/lca-merge.ts`; `--write` would reflow it into a file nobody reviews,
# and a formatter failure here would be a formatter opinion about a measurement rather than a defect in it. **It is
# excluded rather than reformatted, and the exclusion is stated because the last artifact that failed `--check` failed
# after it had been committed.**
benchmarks/lca-bug-localization.json

# **The same rule one artifact over.** `benchmarks/agentic-tools.json` is written by `scripts/agentic-tools.ts` with
# `JSON.stringify(…, null, 2)`, and Prettier's only disagreement with it is that it collapses short arrays onto one line
# — so `--write` here would rewrite 270 KB of recorded choices into a diff nobody reads, and would make the committed
# artifact differ from the file the workflow uploads. **The harness's own output is the artifact**, and the formatter is
# not a second author of it. Verified: the only difference Prettier finds is array layout.
benchmarks/agentic-tools.json

# **The same rule for the second arm's artifact.** `benchmarks/agentic-permissions.json` is written by
# `scripts/agentic-permissions.ts` with `JSON.stringify(…, null, 2)`, so the file a reader sees is the file the workflow
# uploaded. It passes `--check` today; the entry is here so that a change to the formatter's opinion cannot silently
# rewrite a measurement into a diff nobody reviews.
benchmarks/agentic-permissions.json

# **And for the review measurement, whose artifact now carries its own rows.** `benchmarks/aacr-bench.json` used to be a
# page of totals that Prettier could reflow without loss; it now also carries `rankedFindings`, **the per-finding
# features and judge verdicts the next iteration reads** - and a formatter that re-laid those rows out would make the
# committed file differ from the file the workflow uploaded. The same rule as the two artifacts above: **the harness's
# output is the artifact, and Prettier is not a second author of it.**
benchmarks/aacr-bench.json
